Hi,
we are just installing a modem at a True64 system. We want to use ppp via the
phone line. As described in the man pages for modem and pppd, we connected the
modem at ttyd1 and added the following entry to /etc/inittab:
ppp:23:respawn:/usr/sbin/pppd -d +pap -detach /dev/ttyd1 19200
192.168.40.1:192.168.40.100 silent

We connect from a WIN Nt system to that remote system.
For the first connection, it works fine. Then we log out. Now the remote system
does not behave as expected and mentioned in the man pages.
After disconnect, we expect a respawn of the pppd . As we understand, a pppd is
able to handle one connection and must be restarted afterwards. Only killing the
"old" pppd seems to solve the deadlook.
Does anyone have an idea, what to do to get the respawn automatically. We
suppose, the remote modem has to inform the pppd at the remote system about line
closure, but we do not know, what item  to change.

Any hints are welcome. Thanks in advance.
--
with kind regards
J�rgen Grigat


