"Aviv Kfir" <akfir@isdn.net.il> wrote in article 
<3ac2582d@news.bezeqint.net> : 
>I have a card of PDP11 and it has some chips that I don't have a clue about
>them.
>does anyone know what are the DC004 DC005 and DC003 chips ??

From Appendix A of the 1985 Minicomputer Products Handbook (DCK11-AA/AC) Chip Kits):-
DC003 = Interrupt Chip -- provides two interrupt channels
DC004 = Protocol Chip -- provides signals to control data flow to/from four word registers
DC005 = Transceiver Chip -- bidirectional buffer used in peripheral device interfaces
DC006 = Word Count/Bus Address Chip -- 2 x 8-bit binary up-counters
DC010 = Direct Memory Access Chip -- provides logic to perform the handshaking operations required to request and gain control of the system bus.

The manual pages contain a little more info (e-mail me if you want scans), but don't go into circuit details, which are probably given in the Chipkit User's Manual, EK-01387-92. I can't say where you could get this from.

