Most -90 modules with one ethernet port (in this case that would be the
wired port on the AP, either 10Base-2 or -T) _deactivate_ those external
ports when plugged into a hub; the wired connection is made through the
hub backplane.  So yes, to access the wired port on the AP you probably
need to do so from another port on a different hub module, or from the
backbone that the hub is on.

