Well, when the older DEC 3000 machines say the similar thing, it means the
keyboard is unplugged.  It's assuming the system is set up as a server
without a head, so it decides to talk to you on the serial port.  It only
makes this determination on power-up, so if you change the configuration,
you have to cycle the power.

I'm guessing your machine is similar.  I think the keyboard is either not
plugged in, broken, or incompatible.  If you plug a terminal (or terminal
emulator) into the appropriate serial port, you'll see the normal console
dialog.

If the flash ROM was toast, I think you'd see a lot less than this.

