  The current ARC/AlphaBIOS is 4.58-0, based on the firmware website
  referenced in the OpenVMS FAQ.  4.43 looks to be from the firmware kit 
  V3.4 -- the current firmware disk is V5.9 (V4.58-0) and has support for 
  Windows NT V4.0.  The last firmware release specifically targeting
  V3.5-1 was firmware V4.6A, and that provided ARC firmware V4.50-1.

  I'd record the current system configuration and setup from the console, 
  then follow the firmware website directions for the use of the 
  clear_arc_nvram and runecu tools -- this to re-initialize the
  configuration.

