Paul,

The Pentium MMX was never certified (or even designed) for
multi-processor use.  The Intel 200MHz Pentium MMX OverDrive is a
species of MMX.  At the time, Intel wanted to promote the Pentium Pro
for SMP.

One more thing... The processor card in the HX is the same as the one
in the Celebris XL and the Prioris XL.  DEC never even sold a dual
200MHz version with classic non-MMX Pentium, apparently due to timing
problems.  The best you can hope to do with reliability is to run dual
P166s or a single P200 (or a single P233 MMX with PowerLeap).

I have a few unused DEC P166s here as well as the latest 54-24490 CPU
cards and other widgets needed to take an HX system to its designed
maximum... Ben Myers

