> keyboard, even switched SW2 to the serial console position, but I still 
> cannot even get to the SRM. 

The SRM console will NOT work unless there is some memory.  You'll only
get LED codes.

The memory for these systems is MS16-BA (16 MB kit) or MS16-DA (64 MB
kit).  Each kit is 2 matching SIMMs, and the system will take up to 4
kits.  16 MB is probably too little for any modern OS; 32 MB would be
tight; 64 MB acceptable for hobbyist stuff.  Even the smallest kit (16 MB)
would allow you to test the operation of the system.

The catalog described the SIMMs as:
4 Mbit/16 Mbit DRAM technology
Access time of 70 ns
Parity memory technology

These kits show up on ebay occasionally, but they are less common than
kits for the other DEC 3000 systems (400 thru 900 models).  Companies like
Clearpoint (www.clearpoint.com) may have some from time to time.  Any DEC
old equipment reseller might have them.  A number of other companies made
compatible memory.

I don't know if any "common" SIMMs would work in the DEC 3000 300
systems.  I only buy memory if the seller convinces me it will work.
