Correct, the cache on the PPro overdrive is not the same as the PII ... it's
better.  As Eric Smith already pointed out, the cache runs at the full cpu
clockspeed.  The PPro overdrive is basically a socketed Zeon.  It will
outperform the PPro in every aspect.  Unless, of course,  you are doing
something like heavy matrix multiplication which will fit in 1 Mb of
cache but not 512 k and that only applies to the 1Mb PPro.


