> graphics card on the sucker... (it came with the color to BNC connector
> for the VR262 - so it should work -- right?)
> 
> Or do I need a color monitor.

There isn't a color to BNC cable for a VR262.

If you are using a color board, you need a color cable.  Hook the VR262
to the green lead.  Or use a color monitor.

(If the board is an SPX board, you will need to make sure that the
switches are set to 1024x864@60Hz for a VR262.  There is a two switch
DIP switch on the board.  Set both switches either up or down until it
works.)

If you have a mono cable (single BNC pigtail) remove the color board. 
This should put the signal out so that you can see it on the VR262.

