The VX40 is an original Multia.  (166MHz LCA Alpha)

It uses 72pin, x36 (true parity, not logic parity), 70ns SIMMs.  They
are used in pairs.

I suspect that the "ultra small connector" you describe is the floppy
connector.  This machine uses a laptop floppy with flat cable.

To start, I would add some memory, a monitor, PS/2 mouse and keyboard,
power it up and see if it works.

If the battery has gone dead, these machines tend not to boot, so you
may also need to replace the battery.

Good luck!

