>
> Check out the firmware ftp site and web site
> http://ftp.digital.com/pub/DEC/Alpha/firmware/
> ftp://ftp.digital.com/pub/DEC/Alpha/firmware/
>
> Procedure 1
> Your system is not bootable
>
> 1. Power down and goto the IO module and install jumper J6 (fail safe
> loader)
> 2. you insert failsave loader floppy in drive
> 3 power on the system
> 4. system boots up to firmware utility and from the prompt
>     type "update"
>
>     How to create a failsafe loader floppy
>         see the bootable floppy section at
> http://ftp.digital.com/pub/DEC/Alpha/firmware/readmes/as2x00.html
> You basically need the firmware image for the EV4 processor not the EV5
> processor
> put on a bootable floppy.
>
> Procedure 2
> the Alphaserver 2100 firmware release notes has a procedure to upgrade to
> EV5 or downgrade to EV4 , but this procedure requires a working system
> see
> ftp://ftp.digital.com/pub/DEC/Alpha/firmware/v5.9/doc/alpha2100_v53_fw_relno
> te.txt
> Procedure
> 1) Boot the Frimware CD:
>      P00>>> b dka600 -flags 0,a0
>      Bootfile: <cr>
>      UPD> cpu_downgrade
>      UPD> exit
>
> 3) Power off the system.
> 4) Remove the EV5 CPU(s).
> 5) Install the EV4 CPU(s).
> 6) Power up the system.
> 7) Run the EISA Configuration Utility (ECU).



