> a character to the OS. Shift would do equally well in this respect.

A long time ago (1984 or so) I had a co-worker who always hit <RETURN>
to wake up his VT terminal. We kept trying to get him to use the
<SIFT> key instead since the <RETURN> was actually sent to the VAX. To
cure him we started typing

    INQUIRE ANS "Do you really want to DELETE/NOLOG/NOCONFIRM
[...]*.*;*"

on his terminal every time he was going to be away for more than 20
minutes.

It worked :)




