       14th Annual International Internet & Software Quality Week 2001
                    <http://www.soft.com/QualWeek/QW2001>

                             29 May - 1 June 2001
                          San Francisco, California

                     CONFERENCE THEME: The Internet Wave

QW2001 is the 14th in the continuing series of International Quality Week
Conferences that focus on advances in internet quality, software test
technology, quality control, risk management, software safety, and test
automation.

PRE-CONFERENCE-TUTORIALS (Tuesday, 29 May 2001):

  > Mr. Tom Gilb (Result Planning Limited) "Software Inspection For The
    Internet Age: How To Increase Effect And Radically Reduce the Cost"
  > Mr. Erik Simmons (Intel Corporation) "Writing Good Requirements"
  > Dr. Norman Schneidewind (Naval Postgraduate School) "A Roadmap To
    Distributed Client-Server Software Reliability Engineering"
  > Mr. Gualtiero Bazzana (ONION, S.P.A) "Web Testing Techniques and Tools"
  > Mr. Robert Sabourin (AmiBug.Com) "Getting Started -- Stressing Web
    Applications: Stress Early -- Stress Often"
  > Mr. Ross Collard (Collard and Co.)  "Test Estimating"
  > Mr. Thomas Drake (Integrated Computer Concepts, Inc ICCI) "The Quality
    Challenge For Network Based Software Systems"
  > Mr. Bill Deibler (Software Systems Qaulity Consulting) "Making the CMM
    Work: Streamlining the CMM for Todays Projects and Organizations"
  > Dr. John Musa (Consultant) "More Reliable Software Faster And Cheaper"
  > Mr. Gualtiero Bazzana (ONION, S.P.A) "Web Testing Techniques and Tools"
  > Dr. Edward Miller (eValid, Inc.)  "Client-Side WebSite Testing"
  > Dr. Cem Kaner (Florida Institute of Technology) "Teaching Testing: A
    Skills-Based Approach"
  > Mr. Ed Kit (SDT Corporation) "Establishing a Fully Integrated Test
    Automation Architecture"

KEYNOTE TALKS from industry experts include presentations by:

  > Ms. Lisa Crispin (iFactor-e) "The Need For Speed: Automating Functional
    Testing In An eXtreme Programming Environment (QW2000 Best Presentation)"
  > Mr. Dave Lilly (SiteROCK) "Internet Quality of Service (QoS): The State Of
    The Practice"
  > Dr. Linda Rosenberg (GSFC NASA) "Independent Verification And Validation
    Implementation At NASA"
  > Dr. Dalibor Vrsalovic (Intel Corporation) "Internet Infrastrucure: The
    Shape Of Things To Come"
  > Mr. Hans Buwalda (CMG) "The Three "Holy Grails" of Test Development
    (...adventures of a mortal tester...)"
  > Mr. Ed Kit (SDT Corporation) "Test Automation -- State of the Practice"
  > Mr. Thomas Drake (Integrated Computer Concepts, Inc ICCI) "Riding The Wave
    -- The Future For Software Quality"

SIX PARALLEL TRACKS with over 60 presentations:

  > Technology: New software quality technology offerings, with emphasis on
    Java and WebSite issues.
  > Applications: How-to presentations that help attendees learn useful take-
    home skills.
  > Internet: Special focus on the critical quality and performance issues
    that are beginning to dominate the software quality field.
  > Management: Software process and management issues, with special emphasis
    on WebSite production, performance, and quality.
  > QuickStart: Special get-started seminars, taught by world experts, to help
    you get the most out of QW2001.
  > Vendor Technical: Selected technical presentations from leading vendors.

SPECIAL EVENTS:

  > Nick Borelli (Microsoft) "Ask The Experts" (Panel Session), a session
    supported by an interactive website to collect the most-asked questions
    about software quality.
  > Special reserved section for QW2001 attendees to see the SF Giants vs. the
    Arizona Diamondbacks on Wednesday evening, 30 May 2001 in San Francisco's
    world-famous downtown Pac Bell Park.
  > Birds-Of-A-Feather Sessions (BOFS) [organized for QW2001 by Advisory Board
    Member Mark Wiley (nCUBE), <markw@ncube.com>].

POST-CONFERENCE-WORKSHOPS (Friday, 1 June 2001):

  > Dr. Cem Kaner (Florida Institute of Technology) "Developing The Right Test
    Documentation"
  > Mr. John Paul (Minjoh Technology Solutions) "Automating Software Testing:
    A Life-Cycle Methodology"
  > Mr. Robert Sabourin (AmiBug.Com) "Bug Priority And Severity"
  > Ms. Johanna Rothman, Elizabeth Hendrickson (The Rothman Consulting Group)
    "Grace Under Pressure: Handline Sticky Situations in Testing"

Complete information by Email from <qw@soft.com> or go to the QW2001 website:

                    <http://www.soft.com/QualWeek/QW2001>

