> Anyone have any experience with the Intel Pentium II 333Mhz overdrive 
> in dual SMP Digital systems?  There are 100's available on eBay now. 
> They replace the PPro 200.

Paul Repacholi <prep@prep.synonet.com> writes:
> Eh? Given a choice, I'd pick the PPro.

Why would you prefer a PPro over a faster PII that will plug into the
same Socket 8?  The PII Overdrive (socket 8) has single-cycle L1 cache,
so it performs better than the regular slot 1 PII 333.  IIRC it has 256K
of L1 cache, vs. PPro which was available with either 256K or 512K.  So
the only disadvantage would seem to be for CPU-bound jobs that won't fit
in 256K, which are uncommon in practice.

I have a spare machine with a Tyan dual PPro MB, so I'm seriously
considering picking up a few of these PII overdrives to upgrade it.

OTOH, when AMD finally releases their 760MP chipset next quarter,
I'll be in the market for several dual Athlon MBs.


