Paul Repacholi <prep@prep.synonet.com> writes:
> If you are running 32 bit code, the PPro flies. It does suck on the
> 8/16 bit stuff though. The PII was crippled to get get perf up for
> 8/16 bit stuff, thanks readmond! I'd be interested if a 333 does out
> perform a PP200 under linux.

The PII was only crippled by having a two-cycle L2 cache, compared to
single-cycle for the PPro.  The changes to better support 8 & 16 bit
code do NOT slow it down.  And since the PII overdrive does have
single-cycle 512K L2 cache, it is superior to the PPro in all regards
except that some PPros were available with 1M L2 cache.

Compared to a PPro with 256K or 512K of L2 cache, I'd expect the P2
overdrive to *always* meet or exceed the performance.


