Well, I'm the one who made the above statement and I stand by it.  But 
I hardly expected people would compare the binaries of the compilers.
I can change the size of a binary by an order of magnitude with one
additional option.

I meant the complexity of the language meant additional complexity in
the source of the compiler and ergo, the more complex compiler should be
the one that was less to be trusted.

I wold like to see a comparison of the number of lines of code in a C
compiler as compared to an Ada compiler.  And by a C compiler I do not
mean that abomination from Gnu.  I mean a real C compiler.  For example
DEC C vs DEC Ada.  I can even provide the count for a couple of the
early Unix C compilers which were done before people like ANSI or GNU
were able to ruin them.

Of course, another interesting question is, What language is the DEC
Ada compiler written in??  I know what language the real C compilers
are written in.

