Bob, insist that they provide you with an alternate ID number. Medical 
units do not have a defined right to use the SSN as an ID. There are ways 
around it.

The law requires that those that do not have a specific legal need to use 
you SSN as an ID must give you an alternative.

Once you get an alternate ID you will probably experience A LOT OF 
CONFUSION because they will need to reference your previous history. 
There are ways to change those histories.

Here is a link to a document concerning SSNs.:
http://www.privacyrights.org/fs/fs10-ssn.htm

Here is the main link:
http://www.privacyrights.org/

Karl


