> 
> It was working one day then the next was not.  The only confounding symptom
> is that the power and keyboard LEDs are all blinking at about 2-3 Hz.  Any
> contact with the keyboard produces a short chirp but the CRT displays
> nothing.  The particularly confusing part is that even pressing CTRL or
> SHIFT will produce a chirp.
> 
> Does anyone have an idea what happened to this thing?

Seems to be a common problem tith DEC terminals. I've got a VT320
and a VT420 that do this.  I'd guess it's probably a short in
the flyback transformer (DEC seems to use lousy flybacks in
everything).

Open the cover and see if your flyback (big white thing on the 
bottom board with a heavy wire that attaches to the side of the tube)
is cracked open, with black goo oozing out of it (or smoke coming out
of the top of the terminal when you turn it on).

Cheaper to buy a used terminal than to replace it though.
You need to replace the flyback and the large transistor
mounted on a heat sink next to it. Do both at once, or 
they'll just blow again.



