Dennis Grevenstein wrote:
> 
> I don't want to kill my monitor and try all settings, so what
> do I need to set to get the graphic card to work at 1024x768
> at 60Hz.

Set the small rotary frequency switch on the back of the card to '7'
for 1024x864 at 60 Hz., which is supported by the VR299 according to
the PMAGD manual, or to '8' for 1024x768 at 60 Hz.

> Another question: Do these graphic cards work with Ultrix
> or only with Tru64 or OpenVMS?

Don't know about Ultrix.  Definitely still works with VMS up to 7.2
and Tru64 up to 5.1.


