While I partly agree I think it's more important what a language offers than what it prevents. PL design is always a compromise between power and complexity. Preventing from "stupid" mistakes or not to detect mistakes like the automatic type conversions in C++ is a good feature. Java is a better compromise if we only look at the "front end".

> In order for a language to be useable, they invariably provide some "backdoor"
