While I completely follow your thread of thoughts I don't understand the last three sentences. What I understood is that you regard Ada as a PL which has too many safety belts slowing down development. But you stated that this is also a "BAD" thing with C/C++. From the previous sections and from my knowledge preventing the programmer from doing stupid things is *not* a major strength of C/C++.

Basically I disagree. Preventing the programmer from doing bad things in Ada didn't prevent the good programmer from beeing very fast. Ada offers a lot of powerful features which really speeds up implementation. This is a major lack of C - no powerful features.

> Progrmaming Languages are just part of the tool set programmers use to solve
