One point in Ada's favor:  the language has always had an extensive suite
of vaildation tests.  Some subtle bugs have slipped through, which should
then lead to additions to the validation suite.  The expectation is that
any production Ada compiler passes the entire suite, on the specific
platform in question.  This is rather more than most languages offer,
AFAIK.

