I'm not sure what the point is with size of compilers.
Most of the size of the code for a compiler isn't necessarily
related to the complexity of the language.  Compilers use tables
for parsing/lexical analysis.  The tricky part of compilers and
what tends to add size is the code optimizations.

The more a language does checking of syntax and constructs,
the more it relies on data it gets from the sources/includes
(hidden or otherwise).

Compiler size has very little if anything to do with complexity
of the language.  Run-time support may.  The best thing to look at
would be image size for similar tasks having the runtime support
linked in without using shareable images.  Better yet, keep the
task to something done without using libraries and see how much
extra stuff the compiler throws in the final image.


Rick...

