I was not thinking of an open ended winge list to ZK Hoff.

Everyone had their own list of 'must haves', wants, and nice extra
stuff. The common feature is that they are all different... So it
would be nice if we had some idea of what others wanted, and if
someone else was working on it.

It would be even nicer if we started to do some design and engineering
*before* people started cutting code... You know, those things that
under lie WHY we like VMS to start with.

For VMS itself, there is the traditional SIR process.

This is a parallel to that.

So let see if we can do it, and do it well. BTW, that includes
ruthless editing of Subject: and no topic drift folks.

So let's start with the wishlist process. NO 'I want...' yet please.
This is about how we conordinate and plan the whole mess.

